## Replacing the Qt libraries

Use builds of Qt @ERDFLOW_QT_VERSION_MAJOR@ that are binary compatible with the
ones supplied: the same or a later Qt @ERDFLOW_QT_VERSION_MAJOR@ version, for
the same operating system and processor, built with a compatible compiler (see
`THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt`). Replace a library together with the plugins that
belong to it.

### Windows

ERDFlow is installed in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\ERDFlow` unless another folder
was chosen during installation.

- Qt libraries: `bin\Qt6*.dll`, beside `erdflow.exe`.
- Qt plugins: the folders under `plugins\` (for example
  `plugins\platforms\qwindows.dll`).
- `bin\qt.conf` tells Qt where the plugins are.

Close ERDFlow, replace the files, and start ERDFlow again.

### macOS

- Qt libraries: `ERDFlow.app/Contents/Frameworks/Qt*.framework`.
- Qt plugins: the folders under `ERDFlow.app/Contents/PlugIns/`.
- `ERDFlow.app/Contents/Resources/qt.conf` tells Qt where they are.

Replacing a file inside `ERDFlow.app` invalidates the application's signature,
and an Apple silicon Mac will not start it until it is signed again. Signing it
yourself, for your own use, is enough:

    codesign --force --deep --sign - /Applications/ERDFlow.app

### Linux (AppImage)

Unpack the AppImage, replace the files, and start the unpacked copy:

    ./ERDFlow-@PROJECT_VERSION@-linux-x86_64.AppImage --appimage-extract
    # Qt libraries:  squashfs-root/usr/lib/libQt6*.so.6
    # Qt plugins:    squashfs-root/usr/plugins/
    ./squashfs-root/AppRun

The unpacked folder can be packed into a new AppImage with `appimagetool`
from the AppImage project.

### Building ERDFlow against another Qt

ERDFlow can also be built from source against any Qt @ERDFLOW_QT_VERSION_MAJOR@
installation; `docs/DEVELOPMENT.md` in the ERDFlow source describes how.
